  "observations": [
    "The frozen repair service explicitly selects MPExecutor although world_size=1 has a native UniExecutor route.",
    "With both mp engine and mp executor enabled, the frontend-to-model path has ZMQ serialization and a second shared-buffer serialization stage.",
    "MP SharedBuffer slices remaining immutable bytes on send and concatenates immutable bytes on receive once per 1 MiB block. Cumulative copied suffix/prefix volume grows quadratically in payload block count.",
    "The optional linear-copy patch preserves the packet header, pickle protocol, receiver mask, ring buffer, notifier, and 32-block barriers.",
    "Switching to native UniExecutor removes the second process transport entirely and leaves native model execution intact.",
    "The API server forces outer mp engine on. Public PytorchEngineConfig defaults it off, and Engine.from_pretrained supports the native in-process route."
  ],
  "candidates": [
    {
      "name": "uni_executor",
      "change": "distributed_executor_backend=uni",
      "status": "native supported single-device executor path"
    },
    {
      "name": "linear_mp_copy",
      "change": "opt-in process-local SharedBuffer pack_data and _receive_step1 replacements",
      "source_guard": "36d4e3d6100ed469f0381d71d3789e9ce34feaba012823c5c53d464d85fda314",
      "status": "independent candidate; inference validation belongs to root experiment"
    },
    {
      "name": "native_outer_engine",
      "change": "process-local wrapper of AsyncEngine._build_pytorch sets backend_config.enable_mp_engine=False immediately before delegating unchanged to the original method",
      "status": "Independent shim implemented; CPU import, source guards, idempotent installation and no-CUDA-initialization check passed; no GPU validation yet.",
      "constraints": [
        "single GPU, tp=dp=batch=1",
        "native uni executor",
        "same weights, KV, model runtime, preprocessing, generation settings",
        "record effective engine class/config after initialization"
      ],
      "risks": [
        "_build_pytorch is a private bridge and requires source guards",
        "frontend and model tasks share one event loop; host work could increase scheduling contention",
        "must validate startup loop, stream/nonstream response, tail forwards, cleanup, execution evidence and output identity"
      ],
      "implementation": "checks/navigation_latency_inprocess_20261120.py",
      "effective_receipt": "effective_inprocess_engine.json is written only after checking actual native Engine and UniExecutor classes."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Static code paths do not prove the entire historical frontend-to-worker delay is IPC.",
    "Serialization, copies, waits, preprocessing and host/device scheduling need distinct measurements.",
    "Any system optimization must be applied to FP16 as well as quantized models before reporting quantization speedup."
  ]
